cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Steph Speak Bench, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Steph Speak Bench: a benchmark for spoken summaries of terminal output by local LLMs"
abstract: >-
  Bilingual (English, French) benchmark of what a local language model does with a
  terminal command output when the answer is read aloud to a blind or visually impaired
  person: short summary, exact facts, nothing invented, time to first token. Deterministic
  regex scoring, optional LLM judge, standard-library runner for any OpenAI-compatible server.
authors:
  - family-names: Parra
    given-names: Luis
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tutozz/steph"
url: "https://github.com/tutozz/steph/tree/master/benchmark"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - accessibility
  - screen reader
  - terminal
  - summarization
  - hallucination
  - small language models
  - latency
